#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama probe
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:50
#, fuzzy
msgid "Analyze the system"
msgstr "システムの準備"

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama probe (details)
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:52
msgid ""
"In Agama's jargon, the term 'probing' refers to the process of 'analyzing' "
"the system. This includes reading software repositories, analyzing storage "
"devices, and more. The 'probe' command initiates this analysis process and "
"returns immediately. TODO: do we really need a \"probe\" action?"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama install
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:54
#, fuzzy
msgid "Start the system installation"
msgstr "パッケージのインストールを開始しています"

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama install (details)
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:56
msgid ""
"This command starts the installation process.  Beware it is a destructive "
"operation because it will set up the storage devices, install the packages, "
"etc.\n"
"\n"
"When the preconditions for the installation are not met, it informs the user "
"and returns, making no changes to the system."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama questions
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:58
msgid "Handle installer questions"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama questions (details)
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:60
msgid ""
"Agama might require user intervention at any time. The reasons include "
"providing some missing information (e.g., the password to decrypt a file "
"system) or deciding what to do in case of an error (e.g., cannot connect to "
"the repository).\n"
"\n"
"This command allows answering such questions directly from the command-line."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama questions mode
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:62
#, fuzzy
msgid "Set the mode for answering questions"
msgstr "未解決の問題点があります:"

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama questions answers
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:64
msgid "Load predefined answers"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama questions answers (details)
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:66
msgid ""
"It allows predefining answers for specific questions in order to skip them "
"in interactive mode or change the answer in automatic mode.\n"
"\n"
"Please check Agama documentation for more details and examples: https://"
"github.com/openSUSE/agama/blob/master/doc/questions."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama questions answers <PATH>
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:68
msgid "Path to a file containing the answers in JSON format"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama questions list
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:70
msgid ""
"Prints the list of questions that are waiting for an answer in JSON format"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama questions ask
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:72
msgid ""
"Reads a question definition in JSON from stdin and prints the response when "
"it is answered"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama logs
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:74
msgid "Collect the installer logs"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama logs (details)
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:76
msgid ""
"The installer logs are stored in a compressed archive for further "
"inspection. The file includes system and Agama-specific logs and "
"configuration files. They are crucial to troubleshoot and debug problems."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama logs store
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:78
